                                "sense_id": "0ba8292c-ad43-3e8a-8d86-87a3cf7bb1e2",
                                "text": "[…]and therefore that the sergeanty of Easton is to be regarded rather as assistant to that of Scoulton than as partaking of the same rank , that of the chief lardiner of England."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "405ab88e-0979-45c2-8712-e40dd7ae6571",
                                "sense_id": "0ba8292c-ad43-3e8a-8d86-87a3cf7bb1e2",
                                "text": "Indeed, the street called Davygate takes its name from the fact that David Lardiner, the king's lardiner in York but also a knight, lived there and held land in the area."
